<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
     ALLAMA SHIBLI NOMANI
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="aboutshibli" class="h2-section h2-light-bg" data-aos="fade-up">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="h2-section-title">
            <div class="h2-label">The Inspiration</div>
            <h2>Allama Shibli Nomani</h2>
            <span class="h2-divider"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="row align-items-center gy-5">
            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center" data-aos="fade-right">
                <div class="h2-shibli-frame d-inline-block">
                    <img src="~/assets/img/shibli.jpg" alt="Allama Shibli Nomani" />
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-8 h2-shibli-text" data-aos="fade-left">
                <div class="h2-shibli-badge">
                    <i class="bi bi-calendar3"></i> 4 June 1857 &ndash; 18 November 1914
                </div>
                <p>
                    Allama Shibli Nomani was an Islamic scholar, poet, philosopher, historian, educational thinker,
                    author, orator, reformer and critic from the Indian subcontinent during the British Raj.
                    He is regarded as the <strong>father of Urdu historiography</strong>.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Proficient in Arabic and Persian, Shibli was associated with two influential movements —
                    the <strong>Aligarh</strong> and the <strong>Nadwa</strong> movements. He championed the
                    integration of English and European sciences into the Islamic education system.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Shibli established the <strong>Darul Musannefin Shibli Academy</strong> in 1914 and
                    founded <strong>Shibli National College</strong> in 1883. His masterwork <em>Sirat al-Nabi</em>,
                    later completed by his disciple Sulaiman Nadvi, remains a landmark in Urdu Islamic literature.
                </p>
                <div class="h2-shibli-tags">
                    <span>Islamic Scholar</span>
                    <span>Urdu Historian</span>
                    <span>Poet &amp; Philosopher</span>
                    <span>Aligarh Movement</span>
                    <span>Nadwa Movement</span>
                    <span>Darul Musannefin</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

